  "title": "Correct function signatures for buffer functions",
  "description": "While trying to troubelshoot !9596, I commented out `#define\nSOME_FUNCTIONS_ARE_DEFINES` in `wsutil/buffer.h`. It seems that the\nnon-define versions of the functions in question had bitrotted slightly.\nThis updates them with current use, and makes it so Wireshark will build\nand run without that `#define` in place.\n\nIt does *not* remove that `#define`.",
